    [Misc] Install flash-attention-npu in Docker images (#19803)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Preinstall `flash-attention-npu` in the Docker images so the dependency
    is available without a separate manual installation.
    
    - Update `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.a3`, `Dockerfile.openEuler`, and
    `Dockerfile.a3.openEuler`.
    - Build from the `MinghuasLab/flash-attention-npu` fork, pinned to
    commit `9c9f00648fa150e84228a9b757990485fc670df3`.
    - Initialize submodules recursively and configure the build environment
    through the Ascend Toolkit, ATB, and CANN setup scripts.
    - Build in `/tmp/flash-attention-npu` and remove the temporary source
    tree after installation in the same Docker layer.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Images built from these Dockerfiles include `flash-attention-npu`
    by default.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - All image build jobs passed in [Image Build and
    Push](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40432034993),
    including the affected A2/A3 Ubuntu and openEuler images on both `amd64`
    and `arm64`.
    - [CI pre-commit checks and CPU unit
    tests](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/40432035043)
    passed.
    - `git diff --check` passed for the latest changes.
    - No new unit tests were added because the changes only affect Docker
    image dependency installation.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
